cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Heliosonic Sonifier in academic, artistic, or educational
  work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software

title: >-
  Heliosonic Sonifier: Real-Time NOAA Solar Wind Sonification with AI,
  Reinforcement Learning, and a Quantum-Inspired Glitch Engine

authors:
  - family-names: Paquete
    given-names: Hugo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    affiliation: INET-md, University of Aveiro
  - name: DeepSeek AI

version: 18.5
date-released: 2026-08-08

url: "https://github.com/hugopaquete/Heliosonic-Sonifier"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hugopaquete/Heliosonic-Sonifier"

license: GPL-3.0-only

keywords:
  - sonification
  - solar-wind
  - space-weather
  - NOAA
  - reinforcement-learning
  - markov-chains
  - generative-music
  - computational-creativity
  - MIDI
  - data-art

abstract: >-
  A real-time artistic sonification instrument that transforms NOAA/SWPC space
  weather data into adaptive MIDI music through a 7-layer pipeline, 20
  autonomous AI agents, and a quantum-inspired glitch engine. This repository
  documents the system architecture; source code and executables are not
  distributed.

